# The Exsecutor logo's 3D model, rendered by the language it compiles --
# at 512x512, lane-parallel (Stage 5.4).
#
# examples/signaculum/ is three files in two layers. forma.exsc is the PURE
# core: signaculum_pingue(exsg, fb, zb) takes the whole fixed-point
# description of logo/Meshy_AI_Crossed_Ascension_0910024256 -- 1493
# vertices, 2981 faces, baked per-face flat colours -- as ONE 44,801-byte
# buffer (tests/data/signaculum_mesh.bin, written by the producer
# prototypes/signaculum_mesh.py), and rasterises it at 512x512 with a 1/z
# z-buffer, backface culling and incremental edge functions into
# CALLER-OWNED framebuffer (786,432 B) and z-buffer (262,144 f64 lanes)
# borrows, returning a status (0 rendered; 1 bad magic; 2 bad counts;
# 3 short stream; 4 trailing bytes) -- the engine entry point Kiln consumes
# with a ROM, no stream. signaculum.exsc is the stream skin: a pump that
# copies stdin into the buffer, hands over, and writes the binary P6 PPM
# out of the framebuffer. ascensus.exsc is the initium driver. Every float
# the program holds is delivered as an integer on the 2^-23 grid and
# decoded by division by 8388608.0 -- a power of two, so the f64 quotient
# is EXACT on both sides and program and consumer hold identical f64 bits
# from the first operation on.
#
# THE LANE SHAPE (Stage 5.4). The pixel loop's four loop-carried f64
# accumulators (edge functions w0/w1/w2 and depth qd) are acies<f64, 8>:
# each 8-pixel-group step is ONE packed vadd vf64.8 per accumulator; each
# row's lane seeds are one broadcast add per accumulator against the
# per-face offsets lad * step. Coverage and the z-test/store stay SCALAR
# PER LANE -- v[l] indexing -- because the language has no mask shape for a
# conditional store (the deliberate v1 settlement, recorded in forma.exsc's
# header). THE ASSOCIATION CHANGED against the old 256x256 scalar
# per-pixel chain: lane l's value at group g is broadcast(seed) + l*step
# accumulated in steps of 8*step, not the scalar chain's successive single
# fadds -- different last bits, ON PURPOSE, so the golden below is NEW and
# was re-proven whole.
#
# THE RE-PROOF. expected.out (786,447 bytes: the 15-byte P6 header +
# 786,432 pixel bytes; "P6\n512 512\n255\n") was produced from the
# REFERENCE backend's own run and then re-proven byte-for-byte exactly as
# K1 proved the first golden:
#   reference backend (fasmg): byte-identical by construction (the golden
#     IS its output; the cmp is run anyway and matches);
#   the INDEPENDENT certificate, kept (driver decision): prototypes/
#     signaculum_oracle.py was PORTED to the same lane pipeline -- numpy
#     float64 elementwise mirroring the written op order (one IEEE
#     rounding per lane per op), 512x512, same decode, same predicate --
#     and its output byte-diffs 0 against expected.out (system python3,
#     numpy 2.3.4; run.sh never runs the oracle -- expected.out is checked
#     in);
#   C backend, FOUR builds -- gcc -O0, gcc -O2, clang -O0, clang -O2, each
#     `-O$opt -ffp-contract=off -fno-fast-math -fsanitize=undefined -w
#     unit.c tests/c/exsrt_shim.c` -- every run byte-identical to the
#     golden, every stderr empty (no UBSan report);
#   cross: `--hospes mips64-none-o64 --emitte c` + the harness recipe
#     (clang --target=mips64-unknown-linux-musl -mabi=n32 -march=mips3
#     -ffreestanding -fno-builtin -nostdlib -static -O2 -std=c11 -G0
#     -mno-abicalls -fno-pic -fuse-ld=lld -Wl,-e,_start
#     -Wl,--build-id=none unit.c tests/c/exsrt_shim_mips.c), run under
#     qemu-mipsn32: byte-identical, big-endian host proof at lane scale.
# Measured times on the development host: reference-backend run 0.364 s
# (3-run mean); qemu-mipsn32 cross run 0.965 s (3-run mean) against the
# 120 s cross-phase timeout -- 124x headroom. 1024x1024 was rejected not
# on time but on the 8 MiB default process stack: 1024^2 caller-owned
# buffers total 11,579,137 B in one frame. Numbers and the decision are
# recorded in forma.exsc's header.
#
# CENSUS (also in forma.exsc's header): the pixel loop contains ZERO
# divisions -- the only division sites in the unit are in_f64 (the EXSG
# decode, exact by a power of two), iz = 1.0/zv (ONE per vertex), and
# ra = 1.0/area (ONE per face): `grep -c divsd` over the emitted fasmg is
# 3, `grep -c divpd` is 0. `grep -c addpd` is 32: 8 whole-acy vadd vf64.8
# sites (4 row-seed + 4 group-step), each lowered to 4 addpd over xmm
# pairs. mulpd is 16: the 4 per-face lad*step offset vmuls, same fan-out.
#
# NOTE FOR THE DRIVER -- exit status: ascensus.exsc's self-check constant
# is still the 256x256 byte count (196623); at 512x512 the pump returns
# 786,447, so this row reports "got 'exit 1', expected 'exit 0'" until the
# driver's one-constant ascensus.exsc update (196623 -> 786447) lands.
# stdout byte-identity, stderr emptiness, and the audit all pass today.
#
# (No stdout= on purpose: expected.out IS the reference; naming both is
# the run.sh failure for "which of the two governs?".)
TEST: expect-exit=0 sources=examples/signaculum/forma.exsc,examples/signaculum/signaculum.exsc,examples/signaculum/ascensus.exsc stdin=tests/data/signaculum_mesh.bin cross=yes
